  "passage": {
    "text": "The overall structure of a port matters more than any single danger. A port is not one simple workplace. It is actually many organizations working in the same space at the same time. These include the harbour authority, terminal operators, transport companies, and ship crews. Each group has different legal responsibilities. The law can also change within just a few metres. On the quay, national law applies. On the ship, international maritime law applies. At the point where the two meet, both sets of rules may apply together.",
    "cloze": true,
